=== Stats and passives ===

Each item shows Attack and Attack speed as two numbers. The left number is the standard value for that item. The right number is a random offset from it. The catalog lists the lowest and highest each stat can be. The standard value sits in the middle of that range.

A new item can have 0, 1, 2, 3, or 4 passives. Each count is equally likely. 99.2% of rolled passives are ordinary. 0.8% are rare. 40% of ordinary passives are negative. Rare passives raise the suggested sale price. That price is the reference value, scaled by the two stat bonuses and the passives.

Some items always carry one exclusive rare passive. That line cannot be reforged.

Helmets share passives with standard armor. Hats share passives with robes. Negative passives can appear on any item.

=== Inventory and market ===

Collected items go to the inventory. A red lock is a manual lock. A yellow lock means the item is equipped in idle battle. Locked items cannot be sold or fused. Players can showcase a weapon on the leaderboard, sell an item, or open a price chart. Sort arranges the bag by price.

Sell orders list asking prices on the market. Money can be transferred to another player after level 20.

A catalog page lists every item, its min and max stats, and its market chart.

=== Fusion ===

Fusion spends several items of one color to make one item of the next color. The spent items do not have to be the same name. They only have to share a color. Locked items cannot be spent.

